<title>SINGAPORE: Shangri-La to increase loan to Burma firm.</title>
<headline>Shangri-La to increase loan to Burma firm.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shangri-La Hotel Ltd said on Wednesday it agreed to contribute an additional US$1.5 million to an associate company in Burma.</p>
<p>It said in a statement the sum to Traders Yangon Co Ltd (TYCL) as shareholder's loans would be raised by February 11.</p>
<p>The latest loan would raise the total amount of shareholder's loans granted by Shangri-La to TYCL US$20.5 million. The interest-free loans were required to finance TYCL's hotel project in Rangoon, it said.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
